Negative control for the T3.11 preset spec (AC8.5 · S13).

`empty` is the recorded collection with its ROWS removed — the envelope staging
returned, minus its data — never a body written to look like one. This mutant
keeps the empty array and the zero total, and swaps the recorded envelope it is
spread onto for a hand-authored literal. The surface renders identically: an
empty list is an empty list.

What must go red is provenance, not the row count: the recording carries
`related`, `error`, `messages` and `meta` beside `status`, `data` and `total`,
and under the mutant those are gone because the body no longer came from a
recording at all. An assertion that only counts rows, or only reads
`body.data.length`, passes the mutant and proves nothing — the FE-2824 shape that
the data-provenance receipt exists to catch. Compare the served body against the
committed recording's own envelope with its rows emptied.

Bodies must be injected (the spec lane may read the committed recordings
lawfully — eslint 8h).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T3.11 preset spec — the empty case (the answer is the recording
emptied, every other recorded field intact).

Re-armed 2026-08-13: the hunk's leading context is the docblock the two named
error presets rewrote (`R6-19`).

